./packages/i18n/CHANGELOG.md:681:  The move is what fixes the bug. `@object-ui/core`'s `formatMeasure` needed exactly this policy and could not import it — `core` is the React-free engine and is a runtime dependency of React-free consumers (the `object-ui` VS Code extension, `@object-ui/data-objectstack`), while `i18n` depends on `i18next`/`react-i18next` and peer-depends on React. So `formatMeasure` carried a parallel `Intl` implementation, recorded at both ends as deliberate duplication, and the two drifted in the one place a hand-built string and `Intl` disagree. A German session read `1.234,5 %` from a list cell and `1.234,5%` from a dashboard measure showing the same number. The function is pure, so the boundary was never a property of the code — only of where the code sat; moving it down removes the obstacle instead of working around it. `core` imports nothing from `i18n`, so the new edge adds no cycle.
